    --egress                                                         Run the sandbox with allow-listed network egress
    --llm-proxy                                                      Hold model credentials in a host sidecar instead of the sandbox
    --linear <id>                                                    Linear issue id
    --gitlab <ref>                                                   GitLab issue ref
    --project <number>                                               GitHub Projects v2 board number: run every ready item
    --parent                                                         (--linear) Run the sub-issues of a parent issue
    --gc-before                                                      Reap stale sandboxes before starting
    --reuse                                                          Reuse an existing worktree/branch for the task
    --fork <n>                                                       Run the implementer n times (n>=2) and keep the best variant
    --fork-scorer <llm|decision>                                     Scorer for --fork variants (default: llm)
    --spec-file <file>                                               Use this tech spec instead of fetching one (single-issue runs only)
    --skill <name>                                                   Named skill to apply (repeatable; single-issue runs only)
    --help                                                           Print help for this command"
`;

exports[`--help output > skills help is unchanged 1`] = `
"taskcell skills list|check|add <git-url>[#ref]|remove <name>|update [name] [options]

  list | check | add | remove | update the repo's pinned skills; see docs/skills.md.

  Options:
    --repo <path>       Repo checkout to work in (default: cwd)
    --dry-run           Report what would happen without changing anything
    --base <branch>     (update --pr) Branch the PR targets
    --dir <skills dir>  Skills directory (default: <repo>/skills)
    --strict            (check) exit 1 on outdated or modified skills
    --path <dir>        (add) Subdirectory of the source holding the skill
    --name <name>       (add) Name to pin the skill under
    --pr                (update) Open a PR with the SKILL.md diff instead of editing in place
    --force             (update) Update even when the pinned commit can no longer be fetched
    --help              Print help for this command"
`;

exports[`--help output > spec help is unchanged 1`] = `
"taskcell spec <issue ref> [options]

  Write a tech spec for a GitHub issue and post it as an issue comment.

  Options:
    --repo <path>                                             Repo checkout to work in (default: cwd)
    --github-repo <o/r>                                       GitHub repo slug (owner/repo)
    --github <ref>                                            GitHub issue or PR ref: owner/repo#n, URL, or a bare number with --github-repo
    --provider <claude|codex|cursor|zai|openrouter|meridian>  Provider that runs every stage (default: claude)
    --usage-cap <pct>                                         Stop starting work once the provider's plan window is at/over this % (1-100; env TASKCELL_USAGE_CAP_PCT)
    --egress                                                  Run the sandbox with allow-listed network egress
    --llm-proxy                                               Hold model credentials in a host sidecar instead of the sandbox
    --skills <dir>                                            Skills directory, merged with the repo's .github/vanguard-skills/
    --spec-model <m>                                          Model for the tech-spec stage
    --max-turns <n>                                           Override the agent turn cap
    --base <branch>                                           Branch the spec worktree is cut from (default: main)
    --out <file>                                              Write the spec to this local file instead of posting an issue comment (pairs with run --spec-file)
    --commit-author <a>                                       Git author "Name <email>"; also enables white-label mode (no Taskcell branding)
    --help                                                    Print help for this command"
`;

exports[`--help output > stats help is unchanged 1`] = `
"taskcell stats [options]

  Aggregate .taskcell/runs/metrics.jsonl into a cost/token/time rollup (per task, stage, model, probe).

  Options:
    --repo <path>             Repo checkout to work in (default: cwd)
    --branch <name>           Read metrics.jsonl from this remote branch instead (what \`metrics push\` wrote; default: taskcell-metrics)
    --json                    Machine-readable JSON output
    --github-repo <o/r>       Also read each recorded PR of this repo from GitHub: lead times and the LESSONS first-pass rate (needs gh)
    --feedback-authors <a,b>  Extra trusted logins whose review verdicts count for the first-pass rate (as on lessons record)
    --since <date>            With --skills: only runs from the last window, e.g. 30d or 12h
    --skills                  Per-skill rollup: review pass rate, repair rounds and cost with vs without each skill
    --approver                Shadow approver scorecard instead of the cost/token rollup (verdict vs human outcome; needs gh)
    --help                    Print help for this command"
`;

exports[`--help output > top-level usage is unchanged 1`] = `
"taskcell <command>

Commands:
  run                 Run an agent on a task and open a draft PR for review (exactly one of --linear, --github, --gitlab, --project).
  watch               Poll Linear, GitHub or GitLab and run each newly-ready issue automatically (the AFK factory loop).
  doctor              Check whether watch can run AFK before any issue is claimed; takes the same flags as watch.
  review-pr           Review an existing GitHub PR and post a non-blocking review comment.
  research            Research a GitHub issue and post the findings as a comment.
  spec                Write a tech spec for a GitHub issue and post it as an issue comment.
  revise-pr           Apply human review feedback on a Taskcell draft PR and hand it back ready to merge.
  watch-prs           Poll GitHub PRs by label and run the non-blocking review loop.
  doctor-prs          Check whether watch-prs can run AFK before any PR is claimed.
  review-mr           Review an existing GitLab MR and post a non-blocking review comment.
  watch-mrs           Poll GitLab MRs by label and run the non-blocking review loop.
  doctor-mrs          Check whether watch-mrs can run AFK before any MR is claimed.
  stats               Aggregate .taskcell/runs/metrics.jsonl into a cost/token/time rollup (per task, stage, model, probe).
  metrics             metrics push: append this checkout's metrics.jsonl lines to the orphan metrics branch and push (idempotent).
  approve             Compute a deterministic APPROVE/ESCALATE decision for a factory PR; shadow mode (default) never merges.
  lessons             record: distil 0-3 lessons from a closed factory PR or MR; list | dismiss <id>: show or dismiss live lessons.
  skills              list | check | add | remove | update the repo's pinned skills; see docs/skills.md.
  audit               verify | export the hash-chained audit streams (hub, run-events, metrics, decisions, lessons); see docs/audit.md.
  history             One issue's history over the audit streams (trigger, runs, reviews, approver, merge).
  memory              Refresh .taskcell/memory/retrospective.md from run artifacts and print it.
  eval                Run the committed eval corpus and print a per-kind pass-rate report.
  migrate-labels      Rename a repo's old vanguard:* labels to taskcell:* (dry-run by default).
  resume-rate-limited Re-apply the trigger label on issues/PRs a provider limit or an unmet dependency parked, once clear.
  gc                  Reap stale sandbox containers, prune worktrees, and (with --remote) delete merged remote chore/taskcell-* branches.
  hub                 Serve the Inspector UI over HTTP/SSE; "hub rotate-token --token-file <path>" writes a new token.

Run \`taskcell <command> --help\` for one command. Options by command:

taskcell run [options]

  Run an agent on a task and open a draft PR for review (exactly one of --linear, --github, --gitlab, --project).

  Options:
    --provider <claude|codex|cursor|zai|openrouter|meridian>         Provider that runs every stage (default: claude)
    --review-provider <claude|codex|cursor|zai|openrouter|meridian>  Run only the review stage on this provider (cross-provider review)
    --fallback-provider <name>                                       Retry on this provider when the primary one fails (outage, limit, revoked credential); a comma list (codex,cursor) is a fallback chain
    --fallback-model <model>                                         Model for every stage that fell back (default: that provider's default); a comma list pairs with --fallback-provider
    --usage-cap <pct>                                                Stop starting work once the provider's plan window is at/over this % (1-100; env TASKCELL_USAGE_CAP_PCT)
    --provider-model <m>                                             Model for the implementer/simplifier stages (default: provider's default), or a weighted pool: claude/sonnet:3,codex/gpt-6-sol:1
    --review-model <m>                                               Model for the review stage (default: provider's default), or a pool as for --provider-model
    --escalate-model <m>                                             Model for the 2nd and later gate repairs (default: stay on the implementer model)
    --no-simplify                                                    Skip the simplifier stage (lean: implement -> review only)
    --verify <cmd>                                                   Verification command for Proof of Work (overrides TASKCELL_VERIFY_CMD and auto-detect)
    --visual-proof <cmd>                                             Visual proof command for UI artifacts (overrides TASKCELL_VISUAL_PROOF_CMD)
    --conformance                                                    Run the conformance pass (planner-tier model checks the diff against the spec; opt-in)
    --conformance-model <m>                                          Model for the conformance stage (default: same as implementer)
    --commit-author <a>                                              Git author "Name <email>"; also enables white-label mode (no Taskcell branding)
    --plan                                                           Add a dedicated planning stage first (opus, high effort); same as --flow plan
    --flow <name>                                                    Run a named workflow (e.g. flow-b: plan -> implement -> adversary -> repair)
    --base <branch>                                                  Base branch to branch off and target the PR at (default: main)
    --max-turns <n>                                                  Override the agent turn cap
    --max-repair-iterations <n>                                      Override the conformance/verify repair loop-back cap (default: 2)
    --skills <dir>                                                   Skills directory, merged with the repo's .github/vanguard-skills/
    --pnpm-store                                                     Mount a persistent pnpm store, one per repo (see docs/cli.md)
    --feedback-authors <a,b>                                         Logins trusted beyond OWNER/MEMBER/COLLABORATOR
    --repo <path>                                                    Repo checkout to work in (default: cwd)
    --github-repo <o/r>                                              GitHub repo slug for a bare --github number (default: detected from origin)
    --label <name>                                                   Trigger label
    --github <ref>                                                   GitHub issue or PR ref: owner/repo#n, URL, or a bare number with --github-repo
    --gitlab-project <g/p>                                           GitLab project path (group/project)
    --concurrency <n>                                                Max items processed at once (default: 2)
    --egress                                                         Run the sandbox with allow-listed network egress
    --llm-proxy                                                      Hold model credentials in a host sidecar instead of the sandbox
    --linear <id>                                                    Linear issue id
    --gitlab <ref>                                                   GitLab issue ref
    --project <number>                                               GitHub Projects v2 board number: run every ready item
    --parent                                                         (--linear) Run the sub-issues of a parent issue
    --gc-before                                                      Reap stale sandboxes before starting
    --reuse                                                          Reuse an existing worktree/branch for the task
    --fork <n>                                                       Run the implementer n times (n>=2) and keep the best variant
    --fork-scorer <llm|decision>                                     Scorer for --fork variants (default: llm)
    --spec-file <file>                                               Use this tech spec instead of fetching one (single-issue runs only)
    --skill <name>                                                   Named skill to apply (repeatable; single-issue runs only)
    --help                                                           Print help for this command

